# fstab — Libre Computer Le/La Frite (Amlogic arm64) light desktop.
#
# The boot media varies by board + flavor (La Frite: SPI u-boot + USB/eMMC root,
# NO microSD slot; Le Potato: microSD/eMMC). So the .img build rewrites the / and
# /boot entries to PARTUUID= at assembly time (build_img), exactly like the RPi5
# image, so ONE image boots from USB, eMMC or microSD unchanged. The placeholder
# device paths below are replaced; do not rely on them literally.
#
# <device>         <mount>  <type>   <options>                              <dump> <pass>
LABEL=FRITE_BOOT   /boot    vfat     defaults,noatime,nosuid,nodev,noexec   0      2
LABEL=FRITE_ROOT   /        ext4     defaults,noatime                       0      1
tmpfs              /tmp     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec,size=128m 0      0
tmpfs              /run     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,mode=0755        0      0

# zram swap is configured at first boot by the builder's zram helper (the 512 MB
# SKU benefits from it). See build-frite-stage4.sh + RUNNING.md (SKU note).
